// A variant's payload is a written type, and a written type has to
// resolve — even when nothing ever matches on the enum. Until
// `sema_decl.zen` walked an `Enum` declaration, `sema_case.zen`'s
// `cases_of` was the only thing that resolved a payload, and it runs at
// a `.match`; an enum nobody matches on got no rule at all.
//
// position: the payload, not the variant name beside it.
//
// THREE PAYLOAD POSITIONS, NOT ONE. The assertion is the generic "undefined
// name" that unknown_name.zen also makes, so a single position proves only
// that some walk somewhere reached some type — it cannot show WHICH
// positions the enum walk covers, which is the whole subject. These three
// are shapes a walk can each miss on its own: the SOLE variant's payload
// (the `| X(..)` spelling, where there is no second variant to carry the
// walk), a payload on a variant that is not the first, and a payload buried
// in a GENERIC ARGUMENT rather than named directly. `.count 3` says every
// one of them is reached and that none of them cascades.

Sole = | Array(ArrayLit)

Later = Unit | Second | Third(MissingThird)

Nested = | Wrapped(Vec<MissingInner>)


main = (env: Env) Res<i32, AllocError> {
    Ok(0);
}
